DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260606T113000
DTSTAMP:20260524T003326
CREATED:20260513T124855Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260513T124855Z
UID:10001063-1780740000-1780745400@bird-in-hand.com
SUMMARY:Make & Take: Still Life in Broken Glass
DESCRIPTION:Create adorable frameable art from ordinary objects \nTransform bits of glass and other materials into treasure at this hands-on workshop. Local artisan Karen Worst will guide you through the process of selecting the bits and pieces you’ll use to make a charming picture of a flower-filled pot with hand-drawn stems and leaves\, putting the pieces together and\, finally\, matting and framing your creation. \nBefore retiring\, Karen Worst worked as a nurse by day and created art in her downtime. Today\, she makes one-of-a-kind\, nature-inspired art with glass\, recycled glass and sea glass\, acrylic paint and other simple materials. \nReserve your space today! \n$30 per person includes instruction and all material for framed 6-x-6-inch finished art. \n\nDate: Saturday\, June 6\nTime: 10 a.m.\n\nTo save your space: Limited spots available. Call (717) 344-6875 to reserve your space.
URL:https://bird-in-hand.com/event/make-take-still-life-in-broken-glass/
LOCATION:Bird-in-Hand Artisan Village\, 2705 Old Philadelphia Pike\, Bird-in-Hand\, PA\, 17505\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bird-in-hand.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/JuneMT_Header.jpg
END:VEVENT
